---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Equip Solutions Group"
  description="Paul Devine, independent sales representative for SwapLoader hooklifts and StarMix volumetric concrete plants, and an equipment and parts sourcing desk.">

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap page-hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Company</p>
      <h1>About Equip Solutions Group</h1>
      <p>An independent sales representative for SwapLoader and StarMix, and a parts and equipment sourcing desk for everything those two lines do not cover.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Paul Devine</p>
          <h2 style="font-size:var(--step-3);text-transform:uppercase;">The person on the other end</h2>
          <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem;">Equip Solutions Group is built around a simple arrangement: you get a direct line to someone who knows the equipment, has a stake in the outcome, and will still take your call two years after the invoice cleared.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:1rem;color:var(--graphite);">Representing manufacturers means learning their products in far more detail than a catalog shows &mdash; which models are worth the upcharge, where the lead times really sit, and which spec decisions people regret. Working independently means being able to say all of that out loud.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:1rem;color:var(--graphite);">The work splits three ways: hooklift systems, volumetric concrete plants, and a sourcing desk for used equipment and parts. They look unrelated until you notice the common thread &mdash; every one of them is about a machine that has to be earning instead of parked.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ph ph--tall">Photo &mdash; portrait of Paul, jobsite or shop setting<br>Recommended 900&times;1200</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt" id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">How I work</p>
        <h2>Four commitments, and what they cost me if I break them</h2>
        <p>These are not values on a wall. They are the reasons people call back.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">01</span>
          <h3>Fit before sale</h3>
          <p>If a smaller unit, a different model or a used machine serves you better, that is the recommendation. A wrong sale costs more in referrals than it makes in commission.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">02</span>
          <h3>Real numbers</h3>
          <p>Lead times and freight as they actually are, not as they would sound best. When something slips upstream, you hear it from me before you notice it yourself.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">03</span>
          <h3>One thread</h3>
          <p>Quote, order, build, delivery, first parts call &mdash; same person, same phone number. Nothing gets handed off to a queue.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">04</span>
          <h3>Answer the phone</h3>
          <p>Including after the sale, including on a part worth forty dollars, including when the answer is that I cannot help and here is who can.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="plate-grid plate-grid--3">
        <div class="plate">
          <div class="plate-code">Line</div>
          <h3>SwapLoader</h3>
          <p>Hooklift hoists built in the USA, from Class 4&ndash;5 light duty through 50,000 lb capacity, plus the ST-1614 hooklift trailer.</p>
          <p class="small"><a href="/swaploader/" style="border-bottom:2px solid var(--signal);text-decoration:none;">See the line</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="plate">
          <div class="plate-code">Line</div>
          <h3>StarMix</h3>
          <p>Volumetric concrete plants and genuine SMI parts, with operator training and bilingual support. Se habla espa&ntilde;ol.</p>
          <p class="small"><a href="/starmix/" style="border-bottom:2px solid var(--signal);text-decoration:none;">See the line</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="plate">
          <div class="plate-code">Independent</div>
          <h3>Sourcing</h3>
          <p>Used equipment, surplus units and agriculture parts, found through the dealer and supplier network rather than a catalog.</p>
          <p class="small"><a href="/sourcing/" style="border-bottom:2px solid var(--signal);text-decoration:none;">How it works</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark on-dark">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split split--narrow">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Straight answer</p>
          <h2 style="font-size:var(--step-3);text-transform:uppercase;">What independent means here</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <ul class="checks">
            <li><strong>I represent the manufacturers, I do not build the equipment.</strong> Warranty, engineering and production sit with the factory. My job is spec, quote, order and support.</li>
            <li><strong>I am paid on what I sell.</strong> Which is exactly why a wrong-fit sale is bad business &mdash; the referral is worth more than the ticket.</li>
            <li><strong>Not every request fits a line I carry.</strong> When that happens I either source it independently or point you to whoever can actually help.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Start with a phone call"
    body="Fifteen minutes about your application usually gets further than a week of back-and-forth email.">
    <a class="btn" href="tel:+15157200800">Call +1 515 720 0800</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/contact/">Send a message</a>
  </CtaBand>

</BaseLayout>
